Q: Getting result of .Net object asynchronous method in powershell A: <p>Powershell Module NtObjectManager from Google Project Zero does have <code>Wait-AsyncTaskResult</code></p>
<p>It avoids completely blocking the thread (prevents e.g. Register-ObjectEvent -Action not working) by only waiting for 1 second at a time. And the code is short enough to just include in your script if you don't want to depend on the module:</p>
<p><a href="https://github.com/googleprojectzero/sandbox-attacksurface-analysis-tools/blob/852b1586b8c4527f8be3f486801e4830220c76d0/NtObjectManager/UtilityFunctions.ps1#L207-L222" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/googleprojectzero/sandbox-attacksurface-analysis-tools/blob/852b1586b8c4527f8be3f486801e4830220c76d0/NtObjectManager/UtilityFunctions.ps1#L207-L222</a></p>
<pre><code>function Wait-AsyncTaskResult {
    Param(
        [parameter(Mandatory, Position = 0)]
        [System.Threading.Tasks.Task]$Task,
        [int]$TimeoutSec = [int]::MaxValue
    )

    while (-not $Task.Wait(1000)) {
        $TimeoutSec--
        if ($TimeoutSec -le 0) {
            return
        }
    }

    $Task.GetAwaiter().GetResult() | Write-Output
}
</code></pre>
